## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at the edge, multi-modal fusion, and end-to-end latency budgeting across mobile and server.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML, gated multi-modal fusion
- Federated learning, secure aggregation, DP
- Online drift detection, calibration, rollouts
- Data schema for cross-platform signals and privacy controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo forward for gated fusion
function forward(x1, x2, x3){
  const f1 = enc1(x1); const f2 = enc2(x2); const f3 = enc3(x3);
  const z = gate([f1,f2,f3]);
  return head(z);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency budgets in production?
- What privacy budgets would you set for DP in FL, and why?
